<!DOCTYPE DM SYSTEM>
<!-- Pull-down-item help for the ISPF Settings "Log/List -> Log Data Set defaults"
     choice. Shown when the Log/List pull-down is open, the cursor is on that item
     and HELP (PF1) is pressed - DTL <pdc help="loglisthelp">. PF3 returns to the
     open pull-down. Auto-flow (ISPDTLC-idiomatic): no row/col; the title centres
     itself and the conversion utility spaces the blocks. -->
<panel name="loglisthelp">Log Data Set Defaults HELP
  <info>
    <p>The <hp>Log Data Set defaults</hp> choice controls how ISPF disposes of the
       session <hp>log</hp> - the running record of your ISPF activity - when you
       exit.</p>

    <p intensity="high">Process option:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><hp>Print</hp> and delete the data set.</li>
      <li><hp>Delete</hp> the data set without printing.</li>
      <li><hp>Keep</hp> the data set for the next session.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>SYSOUT class and local printer ID apply only when the log is printed.</p>

    <p>Press ENTER or PF3 to return to the pull-down.</p>
  </info>

  <botinst>PF3=Return</botinst>

  <keyl name="HELPKEYS">
    <keyi key="PF3"  cmd="EXIT">Return</keyi>
    <keyi key="PF15" cmd="EXIT">Return</keyi>
  </keyl>
</panel>
